From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuele Bassi <ebassi@igalia.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:36:37 -0700
Subject: Defer XMLDocumentParser::Finish() while inside ParseChunk
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

XMLDocumentParser buffers data that arrives while ParseChunk() is
running into pending_src_, but a Finish() call received during this
state—such as when a navigation body load completes synchronously under
a running script—previously invoked end() immediately and re-entered
the parser before the active chunk finished processing.

Treat an in-chunk Finish() call like the paused parser case by recording
it in finish_called_ and allowing DoWrite() to process completion after
the current chunk and any buffered data are parsed. Additionally, reset
finish_called_ in end() so that DoWrite() and ResumeParsing() do not
process the same deferred finish twice.

Bug: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/553121395#comment8
Change-Id: I8dca1106bf642003351bf56feb15f71c3b0e163e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8419603
Reviewed-by: Dominik Röttsches <drott@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1700858}

